From 1680446f49122b893650fa428056713718f46a7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:53:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(sim): read law (c) band-reach samples through an exact
 XY index

band_reach pooled the island boundary samples of every cut plane and
tested each band disc of each move against the whole set, so a ramp
whose moves each end at their own Z cost moves x planes x samples.

The law reads no plane of a sample, so the set stays one set. A
SampleGrid keeps each sample once by its exact bits and gives each disc
a superset of the samples within its radius; unplaceable samples and
queries (non-finite, far out, too wide) read everything. The verdict
of a disc is a max over pure readings, so the findings cannot move.
The old function stays as a cfg(test) reference; verify::reach_tests
asserts identical warnings on rings, a helix, ramps, leaning moves
(sweep c3), Boundary mode, an empty path and non-finite moves.

Fixes #3588

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
